# Game Architecture Patterns

## Directory Structure

All games follow this structure:

```
src/game_[name]/
├── index.ts              # Main entry (extends ECSExample)
├── factory.ts            # Scene factory
├── constants.ts          # Enums, messages, constants
├── model/                # Data structures and game logic
├── components/           # ECS components
└── [assets]              # Game-specific assets
```

## Main Entry Point

```typescript
import { ECSExample } from '../utils/APHExample';
import * as ECS from '../../libs/pixi-ecs';

export class MyGame extends ECSExample {
  constructor() {
    super({
      width: 800,
      height: 600,
      backgroundColor: 0x000000
    });
  }

  load() {
    // Load assets
    PIXI.Loader.shared
      .add('assets', 'path/to/assets')
      .load(() => this.onLoaded());
  }

  onLoaded() {
    // Create factory and start
    const factory = new Factory(this.engine.scene);
    factory.loadGame();
  }
}
```

## Factory Pattern

Use factories for scene management:

```typescript
export class Factory {
  private scene: ECS.Scene;

  loadGame() {
    this.scene.clearScene();
    this.createEntities();
    this.addGlobalComponents();
  }

  private createEntities() {
    // Use builders to create entities
  }
}
```

## Observable State Pattern

State objects send messages on changes:

```typescript
class ObservableState {
  protected scene: ECS.Scene;

  protected sendStateChange(action: string, data?: any) {
    this.scene.sendMessage(action, null, data);
  }
}

class GameState extends ObservableState {
  private _score = 0;

  set score(value: number) {
    const old = this._score;
    this._score = value;
    if (old !== value) {
      this.sendStateChange('STATE_CHANGE_SCORE', { score: value });
    }
  }
}
```

## Message Naming

Use consistent message naming:
- `STATE_CHANGE_*` for state changes
- `LEVEL_*` for level events
- `PLAYER_*` for player events
- ALL_CAPS with underscores
